<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Uniserv half year results ahead of budget.</title>
<headline>Uniserv half year results ahead of budget.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1996-09-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Half year ended July 31, 1996, compared to year ended January 31, 1996.</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr, attrib (cts)     13.8	  vs    23.6</p>
<p>    Attrib income	   7.32	  vs    12.53</p>
<p>    Pre-tax		   9.35	  vs    7.39</p>
<p>    Tax			 1.94	  vs    3.67</p>
<p>Full name: United Service Technologies Ltd (industrial holding)</p>
<p>    Exceptional gains     nil	   vs    149.79</p>
<p>    Exceptional losses    nil	   vs    140.82</p>
<p>NOTE - Freight forwarding firm Uniserv is a product of a February 1995, merger with Union-Transport Inc.</p>
<p>The group said its results for the latest six month period were ahead of budget.</p>
<p>Uniserv added that its European and Pacific operations had traded profitably and were ahead of targets and that its Americas units was now trading profitably on a month-to-month basis. The African region, however, was been hit by signs of slowing in the South African economy and came in behind target.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
